        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-01T23:04:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "how can we make sure this class is only implemented inside of libbinder and related libraries, so that we are free to change it as more things are needed?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d69fc3090e197520b4c0106dcd82b3f0babc0ed5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18aa276e_8edd232e",
        "filename": "libs/binder/aidl/android/os/IAccessor.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1644679
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T15:50:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we specifically want others to implement this because there are so many different use cases and unique steps to do to go from \"instance_name\" to socket FD.\n\nIf they aren\u0027t implementing this interface directly, I think they will still need to implement other interface(s) that this implementation uses - reach out to authmgr for permission/attestation in trusty case, reaching out to another service to get a dynamic port number (virtmgr in VM to host case) and transport type which might be a dynamic decision (UDS/VSOCK/INET).\n\nAnd if we do that, we end up requirement permissions to connect to the sockets in all of the client processes (other comment thread).",
      "parentUuid": "563bb75f_63db47d3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d69fc3090e197520b4c0106dcd82b3f0babc0ed5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f060b685_99b74583",
        "filename": "libs/binder/aidl/android/os/IAccessor.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-08T12:00:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1. I only made the interface \"android.os.accessor\" available to the virt apex for now. We can add other users later when needed.",
      "parentUuid": "563bb75f_63db47d3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d69fc3090e197520b4c0106dcd82b3f0babc0ed5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d03f397c_43b9b91a",
        "filename": "libs/binder/aidl/android/os/IAccessor.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120458
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T00:12:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should be entirely external to libbinder or entirely internal. I\u0027ve chatted with Devin a bit about this, and we should chat, but it\u0027s not a change in architecture - just a change in where things are.\n\nCan you consider http://go/apis-native-and-idl - libbinder_ndk is already a native API, so we should not add to part of it to be a PL API as well. Let\u0027s chat this week and close this out.\n\nThe implementation of IAccessor should also be in libbinder as well (if not, how will we get rid of libbinder_rpc_unstable later?). This will ensure that libbinder itself knows which FDs it\u0027s opening up and how, and that it can attest them at some level (even if it needs a callback to do something like DICE attestation).",
      "parentUuid": "f060b685_99b74583",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d69fc3090e197520b4c0106dcd82b3f0babc0ed5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a47446f4_8d60742d",
        "filename": "libs/binder/aidl/android/os/IAccessor.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 24,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T13:21:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My initial approach was to expose `IAccessor` only to a limited set of relevant components + libbinder, effectively making it an internal Android interface used among various aosp components. Clients would implement it with their specific logic, such as handling VM connections for Host-to-VM or managing TEE connections and VM authentication for VM-to-TEE.\n\nHowever, I understand from your link that using AIDL for internal interfaces is discouraged. As an alternative, could we make `IAccessor` entirely internal to libbinder and introduce the following API into libbinder_ndk for accessor registration?\n\n```c\nbinder_exception_t AServiceManager_addAccessor(int (*addConnection)(void*), const char* instance);\n```\n\nThis approach allows libbinder to remain agnostic of the accessors\u0027 internal details while avoiding the need to expose both native and AIDL APIs.",
      "parentUuid": "d03f397c_43b9b91a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "d69fc3090e197520b4c0106dcd82b3f0babc0ed5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
