      "writtenOn": "2024-07-10T14:39:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From our discussion yesterday, Steven suggested something similar.\n\n```\nAAccessor* AAccessor_create();\nAAccessor_delete(AAccessor*);\nAAccessor_registerAddConnection(AAccessor*, int (*addConnection(void*));\n...\n```\nThen I think we could do something like:\n```\n// register the IAccessor with servicemanager?\nAServiceManager_addAccessor(AAccessor*);\n// register it locally when there is no kernel binder\nAServiceManager_injectLocalAccessor(AAccessor*);\n```\n\nBut he really wanted to get rind of `int (*addConnection)(void*)` so libbinder can be responsible for creating the FD and calling `connect()` so libbinder controls everything.\n\nCan we break `int (*addConnection)(void*)` apart into multiple callbacks that can satisfy the requirements? So the IAccessor implementation in libbinder can use these callbacks to get the final FD used with `ParcelFileDescriptor addConnection()`.\n\nLike can we get by with `getConnectionInfo` for when we don\u0027t have the connection info at the time of creating the AAcessor, `attestConnection` for authmgr, etc?",
      "parentUuid": "a47446f4_8d60742d",
