      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T15:50:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like that, as the IAccessor impl could effectively control the number of MaxIncomingThreads that way.\n\n1) Are the connected FDs are the heavy part of the connections? Or is it the threads when we start them per connection?\n\nIf we ended up moving to dynamic threading/connections for the sessions is it going to be bad to have 4 FDs (the max the accessor decided on) before starting the threads for them?\n\n2) If we had 4 FDs from IFoo and 4 FDs from IBar, we can still share 4 threads (in the future if/when we implement shared threadpools)? Is it possible to have fewer threads than FDs for the same IFoo interface in that case?",
